# Better CLI Rules

When building or improving CLI tools:

## Output
- stdout = data only. stderr = errors, warnings, progress, prompts
- Support `--json` with envelope: `{"status": "ok|error", "data": {...}}`
- Output must guide the next action — suggest follow-up commands on success and fix commands on failure
- No ANSI codes when piped; respect `NO_COLOR` env var

## Errors
- Semantic exit codes: 0=success, 2=usage, 3=not-found, 4=permission, 75=transient
- Every error: what + context + fix command + docs link
- JSON errors: `{"code": "AUTH_EXPIRED", "message": "...", "fix": "...", "transient": false}`

## Interaction
- Every prompt needs a flag bypass (`--yes`, `--force`, `--name=value`)
- Never hang when stdin is not a TTY
- Progress to stderr only

## Design
- Flags over positional args
- Config precedence: flags > env vars > project config > user config > defaults
- Never accept secrets via flags
- Support `--fields`, `--quiet`, `--dry-run`
- Create commands output the resource identifier

